\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {S2}{\ignorespaces Full model (eddies and viscosity active; ensembles over $128$ realisations at $\nu =10^{-5}$): strain-induced migration of the streamwise and upwash component centroids, each as the ratio of the strained ensemble to the matched no-strain reference, against the rigid-translation law (grey dotted); the shaded bands are the $95\%$ bootstrap confidence intervals of the median ratio. The line configuration is that of Appendix~B of the main text. The components diverge under strain---the upwash held back most---reproducing the qualitative departure-from-RDT mechanism of \citet  {ChenMeneveauKatz2006}. The comparison is qualitative; see text.}}{3}{figure.caption.2}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:s-cmk-aniso}{{S2}{3}{Full model (eddies and viscosity active; ensembles over $128$ realisations at $\nu =10^{-5}$): strain-induced migration of the streamwise and upwash component centroids, each as the ratio of the strained ensemble to the matched no-strain reference, against the rigid-translation law (grey dotted); the shaded bands are the $95\%$ bootstrap confidence intervals of the median ratio. The line configuration is that of Appendix~B of the main text. The components diverge under strain---the upwash held back most---reproducing the qualitative departure-from-RDT mechanism of \citet {ChenMeneveauKatz2006}. The comparison is qualitative; see text}{figure.caption.2}{}}
